    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required that when a newly created owner's computed `customerCode` collides with an existing owner's `customerCode`, a `-<n>` suffix should be appended using the smallest `n \u2265 2` that makes it unique.\n\nI modified `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`):\n\n- Injected `OwnerRepository` into the `service` step (resolved by type per the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions used by the sibling `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` step).\n- After computing the stable `<REGION>-<HASH8>` base value, it collects the set of `customerCode`s already taken by other owners (excluding the owner being created, matching the namesake-count pattern), then appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until the value is unique.\n- Updated the class Javadoc to document the de-duplication behavior.\n\nThis runs within the existing `assignCustomerCode` step of `owners.POST.yml`, before `save`, so the collision check sees the persisted owners but not the in-flight one.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (the collision/uniqueness guarantee) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
